comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-14T04:03:53.093Z","harness:claude-code","Progress (2026-11-14): BeforeMutationHookContext gains a frozen actor block {author, author_source, principal, agent?} resolved by src/core/extensions/mutation-actor.ts from the same resolvers createHistoryEntry uses (resolveHistoryAuthorSource, resolveHistoryAgentIdentity, resolveClaimPrincipal), plus dry_run. runActiveBeforeMutationHooks now takes the author instead of a prebuilt context, so no call site can hand a guard another identity. previewItemMutations evaluates the caller's guards against the staged plan as dry runs with the commit's actor; the unresolved constraint is renamed extension_write_hooks. Two guard bypasses found and closed in scope: commitImportedItem (op import) and pm copy wrote items without running any guard, and commitImportedItem converted every CONFLICT (including a guard denial) into a skippable lock-conflict warning; only the lock acquisition is now skippable. Spec: tests/unit/sdk/mutation-guard-actor.spec.ts (claimant-only close through SDK client, CLI, MCP; preview/commit actor parity; delete dry run, copy, import; test harness defaults)."
  "2026-11-14T05:42:14.567Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 1 (Greptile P1, Codex P1/P2), fixed: (1) commitImportedItem now canonicalizes the stamped document before workflow policies and guards, and the guard, the item file and the history entry share that one snapshot. A guard rejecting the canonical tag sensitive could previously be bypassed by importing ' SENSITIVE ', which serialization then normalized. (2) copy and import guard contexts include body in changed_fields: copy reuses buildChangedFields, and import lists every set field plus a non-empty body. Specs extended in tests/unit/sdk/extension/mutation-guard-actor.spec.ts."
